   <text>
      <body>
         <div type="letter">
                <div type="mainBody">
                    <p>Dear <name type="person" key="syke83">Mr Sykes</name>: Many <seg xml:id="seg1" type="note-anchor">thanks for the corrections</seg>, which I sent off. Yes, it is <seg xml:id="seg2" type="note-anchor">the same translator</seg>. <name type="person" key="joyc05">Giorgio</name> and I leave for <name type="geo" key="G_GBR_LOND">London</name> on <date when="1927-04-03">Sunday</date> or <date when="1927-04-04">Monday</date>. We stay at the <name type="geo" key="G_GBR_LOND_02">Euston</name>. I will write from there.</p> <closer>
                        <salute>kind regards to you both</salute>        	<salute>sincerely yours</salute>                    	<signed>
                            <name type="person" key="joyc82">James Joyce</name>
                        </signed>
                    </closer>
                </div>
            </div> <div type="notes">
                <note xml:id="note1" target="#seg1" type="commentary">See <rs type="letter" key="L_69444">JJ to Sykes 10 February 1927</rs> (<name type="work" key="ID_MISSING">LIII</name> 153-54) in which JJ asks Sykes to “look through” the proofs of the forthcoming German edition of <name type="work" key="W_ULYSSES">Ulysses</name>.</note>
                <note xml:id="note2" target="#seg2" type="commentary">Sykes had apparently asked whether the translator of <name type="work" key="W_ULYSSES">Ulysses</name> (Georg Goyert) was the same person who translated <name type="work" key="W_DUBLINERS">Dubliners</name> and <name type="work" key="W_APORTRAIT">A Portrait of the Artist as a Young Man</name>. JJ responded on <rs type="work" key="L_69450">26 February 1927</rs> (<hi rend="italic">LI</hi> 250) that, “Yes. <name type="work" key="W_ULYSSES">Ulysses</name> has been done by the same man”.</note>
            </div>
      </body>
